# TORGIMA navigation & activation gate

## Two states

1. **Pre-activation** — Erector only (validation). No TORGIMA left sidebar. No Home/Signals/Project/etc.
2. **Post-activation** — After **Launch Direction**: blueprint active, execution unlocked, full platform.

## Locked sidebar (post-activation only)

Fixed order forever — never add/remove/rename/reorder/hide/dynamic/role-based menus:

`Home · Bhudhi · Erector · Signals · Project · Messages · Community · Academy · Reports · Settings`

Left, vertical, full height, same width/spacing/icons. Only **active highlight** changes.

## Pre-activation rules

- Validation Results = **Erector** page → use `PreLaunchShell` (or equivalent), **never** `Layout` sidebar.
- Onboarding / validate / validation/* (except post-launch) → no execution chrome.
- Ask: `hasActiveBlueprint` / launch completed? If NO → Erector flow only.

## Activation unlock

Single event: **Launch Direction** (`launchValidationBlueprint`) → direction anchor, blueprint, plans, signals, condition → sidebar unlocks.

## Refuse

- Showing TORGIMA nav before launch
- TORGIMA nav on validation-results
- Any sidebar structure change when user asks to "improve navigation"

Full spec: `docs/TORGIMA_NAVIGATION_AND_ACTIVATION.md`
